if statement

Executes some code if one condition is true.

<?php
$age = 20;

if ($age >= 18) {
    echo "You are an adult.";
}
?>
. if...else statement

Executes one block if the condition is true, and another if it is false.

<?php
$score = 45;

if ($score >= 50) {
    echo "You passed the exam.";
} else {
    echo "You failed the exam.";
}
?>
if...elseif...else statement

Executes different blocks based on multiple conditions.

<?php
$temperature = 30;

if ($temperature < 0) {
    echo "It's freezing!";
} elseif ($temperature >= 0 && $temperature <= 20) {
    echo "It's a bit cold.";
} else {
    echo "It's warm.";
}
?>
switch statement

Selects one of many blocks based on a variable’s value.

<?php
$day = "Wednesday";

switch ($day) {
    case "Monday":
        echo "Start of the work week!";
        break;
    case "Wednesday":
        echo "Midweek day.";
        break;
    case "Friday":
        echo "Almost weekend!";
        break;
    default:
        echo "Just another day.";
}
?>
